#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Cheat sheet (Herdr popup: alt+h). Any key closes it.
cat <<'TXT'

  SECTIONS (no prefix)                      HERDR (prefix ctrl+b)
  alt+1  main session (orch. / coord.)      w        pick workspace
  alt+2  agents                             h j k l  move between panes
  alt+3  notion (hub) · changes (task)      c        new tab · v / -  split
  alt+4  prs                                t        board in a pane
  alt+5  servers (start / stop / view)
  alt+m  minimize / restore the focused pane (or ctrl+b m)
  alt+0  the hub's orchestrator             i / r    my tasks / my PRs in a pane
  alt+e  Neovim in the repo (find file)     d        lazygit (popup)  · alt+d in a pane
  alt+h  this help · alt+f  switch hub
                                            a        orchestrator · ?  herdr help

  IN THE LISTS                              IN CLAUDE
  enter / double click  main action         ctrl+v   paste image
    notion → sends the task to the orch.    shift+tab  permission mode
    prs    → opens the PR                   esc esc  edit previous message
    changes→ diff in Neovim · ctrl-e edit · ctrl-l lazygit
  ctrl-r refresh · ctrl-o open in Notion
  ? details (prs) · shift-↑/↓ scroll diff (changes) · esc quit

  NEOVIM (LazyVim, space = leader; space alone shows them all)
  space space file · space / text · space e tree · space , buffers
  gd definition · gr references · K info · space c a action · space c f format
  space g D task diff vs base · space g d local diff · ]h [h hunk · q close diff
  space g g lazygit · :q quit

TXT
read -rsn1
